  "categoryApocalipseBlurb": "The book of Revelation, written by John the Evangelist.",
  "categoryApocalipseTitle": "Revelation",
  "categoryConhecerADeusBlurb": "God comes first: the Creator, the name I AM, holiness, the shepherd, and the Word made flesh. Five scenes to draw near to him.",
  "categoryConhecerADeusTitle": "Know God",
  "categoryCristologiaBlurb": "Who Jesus is: God and man, prophet, priest, and king. The trail walks through his person and his work — incarnation, cross, resurrection, and lordship.",
  "categoryCristologiaTitle": "Christology",
  "categoryDiscipuladoBlurb": "Following Jesus day by day: the Sermon on the Mount, family, mission and starting over. Faith that becomes a path.",
  "categoryDiscipuladoTitle": "Discipleship",
  "categoryEntenderABibliaBlurb": "A panorama of the Bible's story: creation, fall, promise, deliverance, the Servant, the resurrection, and new creation — seven scenes of the whole arc.",
  "categoryEntenderABibliaTitle": "Understand the Bible",
  "categoryEpistolasBlurb": "Twenty-one letters to the early churches — thirteen by Paul and eight by other authors.",
  "categoryEpistolasTitle": "Epistles or apostolic letters",
  "categoryEvangelhosBlurb": "Birth, ministry, death, resurrection, and ascension of Jesus — Matthew to John.",
  "categoryEvangelhosTitle": "Gospels",
  "categoryHermeneuticaBlurb": "How to read the Bible with care and faithfulness. The text in its context, the kind of book it is, and Christ's place in the whole story — without forcing a verse on its own.",
  "categoryHermeneuticaTitle": "Hermeneutics",
  "categoryHistoriaIgrejaBlurb": "How the faith reached us: shared life in Acts, persecution, the councils and creeds, and the Reformation that returned to the Gospel.",
  "categoryHistoriaIgrejaTitle": "Church history",
  "categoryHistoricosAtBlurb": "The history of Israel from the conquest of the Promised Land to the Babylonian exile.",
  "categoryHistoricosAtTitle": "Historical books",
  "categoryHistoricosNtBlurb": "Acts of the Apostles — the outpouring of the Spirit and the spread of the Gospel.",
  "categoryHistoricosNtTitle": "Early church history",
  "categoryIntertestamentarioBlurb": "About 400 years of silence between the Old and New Testaments.",
  "categoryIntertestamentarioTitle": "Intertestamental period",
  "categoryLinguasBlurb": "A first path into biblical Hebrew and Greek: the alphabet, root words, and how a translation is made. The aim is to read more carefully, not to replace the Bible in your own language.",
  "categoryLinguasTitle": "Original languages",
  "categoryOracaoBlurb": "The Lord's Prayer as a school of prayer, perseverance and the help of the Spirit. And fasting as a way to surrender desire before the Father.",
  "categoryOracaoTitle": "Prayer",
  "categoryPanoramaBlurb": "The high points of each book in a few scenes. Get to know the whole book before going chapter by chapter.",
  "categoryPanoramaTitle": "Overview",
  "categoryParabolasMilagresBlurb": "The teaching and the signs of Jesus. The parables show what the kingdom is like; the miracles reveal who he is — bread, sight, the storm, life — echoing the Old Testament.",
  "categoryParabolasMilagresTitle": "Parables and miracles",
  "categoryPazNoDiaBlurb": "A breath in the middle of the day: cast anxiety on the Father and walk in trust. Five short scenes for a restless heart.",
  "categoryPazNoDiaTitle": "Peace in your day",
  "categoryPentateucoBlurb": "The first five books of the Bible — the Torah, the Book of the Law, in chronological order.",
  "categoryPentateucoTitle": "Pentateuch",
  "categoryPersonagensBlurb": "Lives that carry the story: Abraham, Moses, David, the prophets, Mary, Peter, Paul. Each trail follows one person across several books, including their failures, and how that life points to Christ.",
  "categoryPersonagensTitle": "Bible characters",
  "categoryPoeticosBlurb": "Poetry, wisdom, proverbs, and songs — arranged by relevance.",
  "categoryPoeticosTitle": "Poetic books",
  "categoryProfetasMaioresBlurb": "Isaiah to Daniel — the longer works among the prophetic writings.",
  "categoryProfetasMaioresTitle": "Major prophets",
  "categoryProfetasMenoresBlurb": "Hosea to Malachi — twelve books; the name refers to length, not importance.",
  "categoryProfetasMenoresTitle": "Minor prophets",
  "categoryPromessaCumprimentoBlurb": "Promises God makes in the Old Testament and the way Jesus fulfills them. Offspring, Passover, the son of David, the suffering servant, and the new covenant, read beside the Gospel.",
  "categoryPromessaCumprimentoTitle": "Promise and fulfillment",
  "categorySistematicaBlurb": "Doctrine gathered from the whole Bible: God, humanity, salvation, the Spirit, the church, and the end of the story — and the thread that ties it all together, from creation to new creation.",
  "categorySistematicaTitle": "Systematic and dogmatic theology",
  "categoryTemasBiblicosBlurb": "Threads that run through all of Scripture: covenant, kingdom, God's presence, holiness, justice, exile and return. Each trail follows one theme from Genesis to Revelation.",
  "categoryTemasBiblicosTitle": "Bible themes",
