  "entryMissionDorAnsia01CentralInsight": "Treasure pulls the heart",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia01HookNote": "The Father's care is the argument against anxiety — not the absence of need.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia01Intro": "Where the treasure is, the heart is. Jesus joins Mammon and tomorrow.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia01Objective": "See how Jesus links treasure, lordship, and anxiety.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia01Title": "Treasures and anxiety",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia02CentralInsight": "Christ is enough in hunger and plenty",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia02HookNote": "Paul's contentment is not stoicism: it is Christ in hunger and plenty.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia02Intro": "Paul learned to be content in every circumstance — in Christ.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia02Objective": "Trade anxiety about having for contentment in Christ.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia02Title": "Contentment",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia03CentralInsight": "There is a shepherd in the valley",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia03HookNote": "The shepherd leads — even in the valley. What fades is not the struggle; it is fear and the sense of loneliness.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia03Intro": "I shall not want — Psalm 23 is trust, not magic.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia03Objective": "Read Psalm 23 as care, not as a charm.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia03Title": "The Lord is my shepherd",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04CentralInsight": "The bread is for today",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04HookNote": "Jesus teaches asking for the day — not the stockpile. The Kingdom comes before the bread.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Intro": "Asking for daily bread is the opposite of anticipating the whole month.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Objective": "Pray the day, not the census of fear.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia04Title": "Our Father",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05CentralInsight": "The inheritance is kept",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05HookNote": "Hope does not deny suffering. It anchors it in the resurrection. Continue in the Sermon on the Mount.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Intro": "Peter anchors sufferers in a kept inheritance — then, the canon.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Objective": "Leave the pain trail for the curriculum: Sermon on the Mount.",
  "entryMissionDorAnsia05Title": "Living hope",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia01CentralInsight": "The story begins with God",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia01HookNote": "The whole Bible starts here: one God, a world made by him.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia01Intro": "The story begins with God making a good world.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia01Objective": "See creation as the starting point of the whole Bible.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia01Title": "Creation",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia02CentralInsight": "The break begins with distrust",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia02HookNote": "The Bible's problem begins with doubting God's word.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia02Intro": "One question from the serpent, and everything breaks.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia02Objective": "Understand the fall as the problem the rest of the Bible resolves.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia02Title": "The fall",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia03CentralInsight": "God answers with a promise",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia03HookNote": "After the fall, God does not give up: he starts the answer with one family.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia03Intro": "God calls one man to bless every family.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia03Objective": "See in Abraham the start of God's plan for every people.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia03Title": "Promise",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia04CentralInsight": "Salvation comes from the Lord",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia04HookNote": "The exodus becomes the Bible's pattern of salvation: God rescues those who cannot save themselves.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia04Intro": "Between the army and the sea, God opens a way.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia04Objective": "Understand the exodus as the picture of salvation the Bible repeats.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia04Title": "Rescue",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia05CentralInsight": "Someone carries the guilt in our place",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia05HookNote": "Centuries before Jesus, Isaiah describes a Servant who carries the people's guilt.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia05Intro": "A prophet sees someone wounded in the place of others.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia05Objective": "See how the prophets point to a Savior who suffers.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia05Title": "The Servant",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia06CentralInsight": "Death does not have the last word",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia06HookNote": "Everything before meets here: Jesus defeats the death that came in with the fall.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia06Intro": "The tomb is empty. The story turns.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia06Objective": "Understand the resurrection as the center of the Bible's story.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia06Title": "Resurrection",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia07CentralInsight": "God makes all things new",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia07HookNote": "The Bible opens with a garden and closes with a city. God remakes what the fall broke.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia07Intro": "The story ends where it began: God with his people.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia07Objective": "See the end of the Bible as the restoring of the beginning.",
  "entryMissionEntradaBiblia07Title": "New creation",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus01CentralInsight": "God comes before everything",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus01HookNote": "The Bible's first sentence is not about us: it is about God, who creates.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus01Intro": "Before everything, God. The Bible starts with who he is.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus01Objective": "See that knowing God starts with him, not with us.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus01Title": "In the beginning, God",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus02CentralInsight": "God makes himself known by name",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus02HookNote": "Moses asks who is sending him. God answers with a name that depends on no one.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus02Intro": "At the bush, God tells a fugitive his name.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus02Objective": "Understand what the name I AM reveals about God.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus02Title": "I AM",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus03CentralInsight": "God is holy",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus03HookNote": "God is not a bigger version of us. Holiness is what sets him apart from everything.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus03Intro": "Isaiah sees the Lord on the throne, and the temple shakes.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus03Objective": "See why God's holiness changes whoever comes near him.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus03Title": "Holy, holy, holy",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus04CentralInsight": "The Holy One cares up close",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus04HookNote": "David calls the God of the throne a shepherd. The Holy One does not stay far away.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus04Intro": "The holy God also cares up close.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus04Objective": "Connect God's holiness to his care in everyday life.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus04Title": "The Lord is my shepherd",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus05CentralInsight": "In Jesus, God came near",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus05HookNote": "John starts like Genesis: “In the beginning”. Now the Creator comes to live among us.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus05Intro": "In Jesus, God comes closer than ever.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus05Objective": "See in Jesus the clearest way to know God.",
  "entryMissionEntradaDeus05Title": "The Word became flesh",
