  "profileYourJourney": "Your journey",
  "promiseTrail01Intro": "It all starts with a promise: land, offspring, and blessing for all the families of the earth. Follow that thread from Abraham to Christ.",
  "promiseTrail01Note": "God promises a childless man that through him all the families of the earth will be blessed.",
  "promiseTrail01Title": "In you, all the families",
  "promiseTrail02Intro": "Abram still has no son. God takes him outside and tells him to look at the sky.",
  "promiseTrail02Note": "Abram believed, and it was counted to him as righteousness. Paul will come back to this verse.",
  "promiseTrail02Title": "Count the stars",
  "promiseTrail03Intro": "The son of the promise climbs the mountain. The promise seems at risk.",
  "promiseTrail03Note": "On Moriah, God provides the lamb in the son's place and confirms the promise with an oath.",
  "promiseTrail03Title": "The Lord will provide",
  "promiseTrail04Intro": "Centuries later, Abraham's family is an enslaved people in Egypt. The promise seems dead. God has not forgotten.",
  "promiseTrail04Note": "God introduces himself as the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob: the old promise drives the rescue.",
  "promiseTrail04Title": "God remembers",
  "promiseTrail05Intro": "Free from Egypt, the people reach Sinai. The promise takes the shape of a covenant.",
  "promiseTrail05Note": "Israel will be a kingdom of priests: Abraham's blessing passes through a people to reach the nations.",
  "promiseTrail05Title": "A people for the nations",
  "promiseTrail06Intro": "Now in the land, Joshua retells the story and calls the people to choose whom they will serve.",
  "promiseTrail06Note": "The land was given; the people's faithfulness will fail. The promise will need someone greater than Israel.",
  "promiseTrail06Title": "In the promised land",
  "promiseTrail07Intro": "The people fail, but God does not give up. Now the promise narrows to a king: David.",
  "promiseTrail07Note": "God chooses the youngest of Jesse's sons. From David's line will come the king whose throne will have no end (2 Samuel 7).",
  "promiseTrail07Title": "The chosen king",
  "promiseTrail08Intro": "The prophets announce someone who carries the guilt of others.",
  "promiseTrail08Note": "As on Moriah, someone takes another's place: the Servant is wounded for our transgressions.",
  "promiseTrail08Title": "The wounded Servant",
  "promiseTrail09Intro": "The Sinai covenant was broken. God promises another.",
  "promiseTrail09Note": "God promises to write the law on the heart and forgive sin. Jesus will call the cup of the supper the new covenant.",
  "promiseTrail09Title": "A new covenant",
  "promiseTrail10Intro": "Matthew opens the New Testament with Jesus, son of David, son of Abraham. The thread reaches a person.",
  "promiseTrail10Note": "Immanuel, God with us: the son promised to Abraham and the king promised to David are the same.",
  "promiseTrail10Title": "Son of David, son of Abraham",
  "promiseTrail11Intro": "The fulfillment arrives small: in a manger, announced to shepherds.",
  "promiseTrail11Note": "The great joy is for all the people: an echo of the blessing promised to all the families of the earth.",
  "promiseTrail11Title": "Joy for all the people",
  "promiseTrail12Intro": "Paul ties the thread: the promise made to Abraham reaches those who believe.",
  "promiseTrail12Note": "In Christ, Abraham's blessing reaches the nations by faith. And the promise still points to the new creation.",
  "promiseTrail12Title": "The blessing reaches you",
